Package: fessel-monitor
Version: @VERSION@
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-pydantic, python3-paho-mqtt, python3-yaml, python3-fastapi, python3-uvicorn, python3-uvloop, python3-httptools, python3-websockets, python3-watchfiles, python3-httpx, python3-gi, python3-numpy, python3-opencv, gir1.2-gst-plugins-bad-1.0, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-alsa, gstreamer1.0-tools, mosquitto, v4l-utils
Maintainer: Fessel <noreply@example.com>
Description: Fessel robot-arm monitoring (Pi side)
 supervisor (safety/control plane + MQTT relay), video (GStreamer pipeline +
 live state machine + ring buffer + explicit recordings), and uploader (PUTs
 flagged recordings to webui-backend's recording-ingest endpoint over the
 tailnet), shipped as system-integrated Python modules under /opt/fessel/lib
 relying on Debian python3-* packages (no venv), with launcher wrappers in
 /usr/bin and their systemd units. The uploader is an HTTPS client only
 (python3-httpx, in Depends) and holds no cluster-store credentials — auth is
 by Tailscale identity (Slice 5.5). Configuration lives in /etc/fessel and is
 preserved across upgrades.
